The Nautilus DevOps team is diving into Kubernetes for application management. 
One team member has a task to create a pod according to the details below:

Create a pod named pod-nginx using the nginx image with the latest tag. Ensure to specify the tag as nginx:latest.

Set the app label to nginx_app, and name the container as nginx-container.

Note: The kubectl utility on the jump-host has been configured to work with the Kubernetes cluster.

SOLUTION
Pod YAML Manifest
yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: pod-nginx
  labels:
    app: nginx_app
spec:
  containers:
  - name: nginx-container
    image: nginx:latest
Steps to Create the Pod
Option 1: Create using a YAML file
Create the YAML file:

bash
cat <<EOF > pod-nginx.yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: pod-nginx
  labels:
    app: nginx_app
spec:
  containers:
  - name: nginx-container
    image: nginx:latest
EOF
Apply the manifest:

bash
kubectl apply -f pod-nginx.yaml
Option 2: Create using imperative command
bash
kubectl run pod-nginx --image=nginx:latest --labels="app=nginx_app" --dry-run=client -o yaml | \
  sed 's/name: pod-nginx/name: pod-nginx\n  labels:\n    app: nginx_app/' > /dev/null
The cleaner imperative approach is to generate the manifest and modify it:

bash
kubectl run pod-nginx --image=nginx:latest --labels="app=nginx_app" --dry-run=client -o yaml > pod-nginx.yaml
Then edit the file to change the container name from pod-nginx to nginx-container:

yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  labels:
    app: nginx_app
  name: pod-nginx
spec:
  containers:
  - image: nginx:latest
    name: nginx-container
Then apply:

bash
kubectl apply -f pod-nginx.yaml
Verification
After creating the pod, verify it's running correctly:

bash
# Check pod status
kubectl get pod pod-nginx

# Get detailed information
kubectl describe pod pod-nginx

# Verify labels
kubectl get pod pod-nginx --show-labels

# Verify the container name and image
kubectl get pod pod-nginx -o jsonpath='{.spec.containers[*].name}{"\n"}{.spec.containers[*].image}{"\n"}'
Expected output should show:

Pod name: pod-nginx

Label: app=nginx_app

Container name: nginx-container

Image: nginx:latest

Status: Running

Summary of Requirements Met
Requirement	Value
Pod name	pod-nginx
Image	nginx:latest
Label	app=nginx_app
Container name	nginx-container
The pod is now created with all the specified requirements.

